    "intro_html":  "Wild rice is not really rice, it is a marsh grass that Minnesota has been harvesting by canoe for centuries, and it tastes like nothing else in the grain aisle. Here it goes into a creamy turkey bake with mushrooms, celery, and Swiss cheese. Each serving carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). That is one of the pricier dishes in this batch, and the wild rice is the reason. It is also the reason it tastes like a supper club instead of a casserole.",
